                     /note="Belongs to the Ser/Thr family of protein kinases.
                     Experimental studies show evidence of auto-phosphorylation
                     on serine/threonine residues. PknB has been shown to be a
                     substrate for PstP and its kinase activity is affected by
                     PstP-mediated dephosphorylation. PknB and PstP (Rv0018c)
                     may act as a functional pair in vivo to control
                     mycobacterial cell growth."
