                     /gene="higB"
                     /locus_tag="Rv1955"
                     /note="part of toxin-antitoxin (TA) operon with Rv1956.
                     Upon expression in E. coli has been shown to function as
                     an antitoxin against Rv1956 (PubMed: 19016878); It is not
                     clear if these conflicting results are due to expression
                     in a heterologous system; In various publications, both
                     gene names higA and higB have been assigned to both Rv1955
                     and Rv1956; we have chosen to call Rv1955 higB after
                     consulting the authors."
                     /codon_start=1
                     /transl_table=11
                     /product="toxin HigB"
